; voice-track-worker-run.fk — the voice-track SERVICE: one tongue's pieces, rendered by the body's own mouth from the body's own tables.
; The host's manager runs this (docs/launchd/earth.hati.voice-track-worker.plist: launchd KeepAlive restarts it when it dies or is ended);
; the body never begins it. It waits for a request -- the tongue named in .hearth/voice-track/worker.request, which the supervisor
; (voice-track-run.fk) writes -- renders that tongue's pieces under the machine-wide GPU lease (resumable: a piece already rendered is not
; rendered again), says "done", and waits for the next. Its progress is a record in the shared field (voice-track-record.bml: pid, seq,
; stage, done, total, begun_ms, beat_ms, state), given when a piece begins and when it lands; the supervisor reads that, and ends this
; process with host_signal if it has been "working" with no beat for VTRIdleMs.
; Proof: tests/voice-track-service-band.fk (the record protocol, the stall decision, no begun process); the 2026-10-03 run of all four
; tongues (receipts/2026-10-03-the-voice-spoke-without-leaving-the-body.md) rendered with the worker this replaces.
; The worker holds the GPU lease (/tmp/form-gpu.lock, machine-wide, gpu-lease.bml) for the length of one request -- vtr-leased-work -- and the
; supervisor (voice-track.bml) does not: a worker the supervisor ends leaves a dead owner's lease, and the next worker takes it over.
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/voice-track.bml
(do
    (vtr-serve)
    0)
